size-buffers: fluid model in 10 us steps. Illustrative, not a measurement.
stack             kernel
arrival           idle 0.000 Mpps, burst 10.000 Mpps for 100000 us from 0 us
stage 1           RX ring: 1000000 packets, drained at 1.000 Mpps
stage 2           socket buffer: 92 packets (212992 B at 2304 B each), read at 0.000 Mpps
reader pause      none

dropped, stage 1  0 packets (rx_missed_errors)
dropped, stage 2  999908 packets (UdpRcvbufErrors)
first drop        stage 2 at 90 us
peak fill         stage 1: 900000 of 1000000, stage 2: 92 of 92

To lose nothing in this scenario:
unbounded         the queues do not empty within 2 s of simulated time, so no finite size is enough
ring memory now   2000000 KiB per queue, 2000000 KiB for 1 queue(s)
